Phoebe Buffay?

266
00:18:09,920 --> 00:18:11,750
Fire Alarm?

267
00:18:16,920 --> 00:18:20,720
Oh, hi, Officer Fireman. Can I help you?

268
00:18:20,930 --> 00:18:22,850
Your fire alarm was in the trash.

269
00:18:23,180 --> 00:18:24,930
That's not mine.

270
00:18:23,180 --> 00:18:24,930
Yes, it is.

271
00:18:25,100 --> 00:18:26,100
How do you know?

272
00:18:26,270 --> 00:18:29,230
If you dump a fire alarm, don't use a blanket that says:

273
00:18:29,480 --> 00:18:32,400
"Property of Phoebe Buffay, not Monica."

274
00:18:33,400 --> 00:18:35,110
Do you have a search warrant?

275
00:18:35,320 --> 00:18:38,780
Because the last time I checked, this was still America.

276
00:18:39,910 --> 00:18:42,910
Please reattach it. It's against the law to disconnect them.

277
00:18:43,120 --> 00:18:47,200
Fine. But please, God, tell me how to stop it from going off?

278
00:18:47,410 --> 00:18:49,000
Press the reset button.

279
00:18:49,210 --> 00:18:52,830
There's a reset button? Oh, thank you. Thank you.

280
00:18:53,040 --> 00:18:55,920
Oh. There's a reset button?

281
00:18:56,170 --> 00:18:58,170
My God!

282
00:18:58,420 --> 00:18:59,970
Why didn't I see that?

283
00:19:02,390 --> 00:19:04,970
Reset button. Reset button.

284
00:19:05,220 --> 00:19:08,390
Where is there a reset button? Oh, here it is! Oh!

285
00:19:21,030 --> 00:19:22,990
God!

286
00:19:27,040 --> 00:19:29,660
Okay, you have a good grip?

287
00:19:27,040 --> 00:19:29,660
Yeah.

288
00:19:29,870 --> 00:19:32,710
Okay, I'm gonna start to climb down you now.

289
00:19:35,750 --> 00:19:37,670
All right, just hurry up.

290
00:19:35,750 --> 00:19:37,670
Okay.

291
00:19:37,880 --> 00:19:41,300
Now, should I climb down your front so we're face to face...

292
00:19:41,510 --> 00:19:45,010
...or should I climb down your back so we're...

293
00:19:45,220 --> 00:19:46,970
...butt to face?

294
00:19:48,310 --> 00:19:50,680
Face to face.

295
00:19:48,310 --> 00:19:50,680
I like face to face.

296
00:19:51,440 --> 00:19:54,400
Okay, here I come.

297
00:19:51,440 --> 00:19:54,400
All right.

298
00:19:57,610 --> 00:20:00,360
Oh, my... How much do you weigh, Ross?

299
00:20:01,530 --> 00:20:06,490
I prefer not to answer that right now. I'm still carrying a little holiday weight.

300
00:20:14,080 --> 00:20:16,330
When we talked about face to face...

301
00:20:16,540 --> 00:20:19,420
...I don't think we thought it all the way through.

302
00:20:20,050 --> 00:20:23,880
What do you want me to do?

303
00:20:20,050 --> 00:20:23,880
Just shimmy down me and drop.

304
00:20:29,140 --> 00:20:30,680
Hi.

305
00:20:29,140 --> 00:20:30,680
Hi.

306
00:20:32,430 --> 00:20:36,060
You know, maybe I should hang, and you should climb down me.

307
00:20:36,270 --> 00:20:39,860
Yeah? Maybe we should talk about that for a little while!

308
00:20:41,320 --> 00:20:44,990
It still looks pretty far.

309
00:20:41,320 --> 00:20:44,990
It's not that far. Just drop.

310
00:20:45,200 --> 00:20:46,950
Do not rush me!

311
00:20:54,960 --> 00:20:59,710
Ross, my pants are starting to come down, and I'm not wearing any underwear.

312
00:21:01,840 --> 00:21:02,840
Whoa!

313
00:21:04,300 --> 00:21:07,800
Ow! My ankle! I really hurt my ankle!

314
00:21:08,050 --> 00:21:11,560
I think I twisted it when... Ooh, a quarter!

315
00:21:17,350 --> 00:21:19,770
That really was some of your best work.

316
00:21:19,980 --> 00:21:21,190
I told you.

317
00:21:25,320 --> 00:21:26,490
I can't believe it.

318
00:21:26,700 --> 00:21:30,830
I've only got two hours until I call in sick for work.

319
00:21:31,290 --> 00:21:33,330
I have to be up in seven minutes.

320
00:21:34,370 --> 00:21:38,540
Well, you're not gonna believe this, but if you have seven minutes...

321
00:21:39,250 --> 00:21:40,840
Really?

322
00:21:41,340 --> 00:21:42,750
You want to?

323
00:21:42,960 --> 00:21:46,420
Okay. You get the vacuum cleaner. I'll get the furniture polish.

